CJSON_PUBLIC(int) cJSON_GetArraySize(const cJSON *array);
    ```
16. `cJSON_free`
    `cJSON_free` is the library’s deallocation wrapper. Use it to free memory previously allocated by cJSON or by the hooks’ allocator. It simply calls `global_hooks.deallocate(object)`. Passing `NULL` is safe if the underlying deallocator is. Its signature is:
    ```c
    
CJSON_PUBLIC(void) cJSON_free(void *object);
    ```
17. `cJSON_GetStringValue`
    `cJSON_GetStringValue` is a safe accessor for string items. Use it on a `cJSON*` when you expect a JSON string; it returns `item->valuestring`. If `item` is not a string (or is NULL), it returns `NULL`. Its signature is:
    ```c
